{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":592.6900024414062,"text":"pushing the fraud detection rate much higher, but at the end of the day, the downstream task was to say, here's the sequence of transactions. I have someone just using the debit card. Is that transaction fraudulent with respect to all historical information? And that's exactly what you put in at inference time when you try to do the prediction. So that's the architecture. So nothing really fancy here. You just need to have the good engineering in place to do less than 250 milliseconds for doing the processing, because the decline needs to happen within that time frame. But we were, well, 10 times slower than that from a latency perspective. So it was all good. And just in terms of final result we get. So the main metrics, and those metrics relate right away to savings for the firm. So it's detection rate and false positive rate. Of course, you can detect much higher, but in many cases, sometimes you get much more false positive. And in this case, we managed to get, we flag more fraudulent activities, and we even reduced the false positive. So that was a big win. That was a big win, because at the end of the day, if you decline a transaction which is not fraudulent, then that person is going to call, there is an operation cost associated to it, you lose the transaction related to that non-fraudulent action. So it's a very, well, something that you don't really want to happen. So again, that's compared to the state of the art of the G-Boost model using fraud detection. So it's basically huge. It's millions of dollar savings. So it's a very big boost. So just to finish up on that slide, so that foundation model has been built on billions of transactions from Wells Fargo customers. That's number one. It's pre-trained from scratch. So we don't pre-train from any open rate existing model. We use existing architecture, but the way the zero rate, we pre-train it on a couple of days. I mean, we did it on a couple of weeks initially, but then that's pre-trained. And then when it's pre-trained, it's pretty good in predicting the next transaction. Then when you're done with that, then you can use it for many downstream tasks. We did it for fraud detection. Now we're investigating for credit line increase, investigating for anti-money laundering, investigating for marketing. So now the same foundation is used across different organizations, even in Wells Fargo. And yeah, thank you for having me and thank you.","segments":[{"id":0,"seek":0,"start":0.0,"end":3.8399999141693115,"text":" pushing the fraud detection rate much higher, but at the end of the day, the downstream","tokens":[50364,7380,264,14560,17784,3314,709,2946,11,457,412,264,917,295,264,786,11,264,30621,50556],"temperature":0.0,"avg_logprob":-0.3313938081264496,"compression_ratio":1.6489795446395874,"no_speech_prob":0.2829723060131073},{"id":1,"seek":0,"start":3.8399999141693115,"end":7.139999866485596,"text":" task was to say, here's the sequence of transactions.","tokens":[50556,5633,390,281,584,11,510,311,264,8310,295,16856,13,50721],"temperature":0.0,"avg_logprob":-0.3313938081264496,"compression_ratio":1.6489795446395874,"no_speech_prob":0.2829723060131073},{"id":2,"seek":0,"start":7.139999866485596,"end":9.880000114440918,"text":" I have someone just using the debit card.","tokens":[50721,286,362,1580,445,1228,264,39709,2920,13,50858],"temperature":0.0,"avg_logprob":-0.3313938081264496,"compression_ratio":1.6489795446395874,"no_speech_prob":0.2829723060131073},{"id":3,"seek":0,"start":9.880000114440918,"end":16.15999984741211,"text":" Is that transaction fraudulent with respect to all historical information?","tokens":[50858,1119,300,14425,14560,23405,365,3104,281,439,8584,1589,30,51172],"temperature":0.0,"avg_logprob":-0.3313938081264496,"compression_ratio":1.6489795446395874,"no_speech_prob":0.2829723060131073},{"id":4,"seek":0,"start":16.15999984741211,"end":23.760000228881836,"text":" And th